  "notes": "SHARP 2T-C32GH3000I (reported as SHARP 2K Smart TV-A; Skyworth-built, device beomil, product SW11_SHARP_APEU, MediaTek mt5867), Indonesia\nGoogle TV 14 (API 34), build UKN6.260116.061, ~1 GB RAM. Same platform as motorola-swtv-24ae-fhd.\nStock launcher: com.google.android.apps.tv.launcherx (Google TV).\nSetup wizard: com.google.android.tungsten.setupwraith (claims HOME).\nLive TV app: com.cltv.hybrid; HDMI and tuner inputs: com.mediatek.tvinput.\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/sharp-2t-c32gh3000i/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/sharp-2t-c32gh3000i/debloat.txt com.google.android.apps.tv.launcherx\nEverything is DISABLED for user 0, never uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nPort 5555 was closed out of the box; only Wireless debugging was offered, so the first connection\nwas `adb pair` + `adb connect` + `adb tcpip 5555`.\n\nWARNING: on this set the Wi-Fi network joined during first setup belonged to setupwraith\n(`dumpsys wifi | grep -o 'cname=[^ ]*'`). Forget it and re-join it in Settings before disabling\nsetupwraith, or Android deletes the network and the TV drops off Wi-Fi.\n\nApplied and verified on 2026-10-21: screenshots after each batch, a reboot (nothing came back),\nLive TV, HDMI and YouTube/Netflix playback; the real remote's Home, Input, Settings and app buttons\nall worked with INPUT_KEY_SERVICE=1 HOME_KEY_SERVICE=1 and settings_key_keycodes 83.\nLauncher config: live_tv_package com.cltv.hybrid (also hidden from the grid).\nPrivate DNS works on this set (streams buffered with AdGuard on this ISP, not with Cloudflare).\nVoice search for content (\"open YouTube to search ...\") fails with `provider.OPEN ... UNKNOWN_ERROR`\nonce launcherx is off (docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md); app commands (\"open YouTube\") still work. Kept off.\n\nKept on purpose: com.smartdevice.global.service (global keys, BLE remote, find-my-remote),\ncom.smartdevice.dailyshortcut (GLOBAL_BUTTON receiver), com.tianci.localmedia (USB media player),\ncom.google.android.tv.googletvremotepairer (remote pairing), com.smartdevice.factory (never launched),\ncom.cltv.hybrid, com.mediatek.*, Play Store, Play Services, Gboard, Google TTS, Dolby audio,\ncom.google.android.katniss (voice, by choice), com.google.android.tv.remote.service (phone remote, by choice),\ncom.tcl.browser (this is BrowseHere, by choice).\n--- Skyworth telemetry and activation ---",
